From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zuohuiyang <zuohuiyang@foxmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:15:00 +0800
Subject: perf: avoid unused address and DNS metadata in Windows network lists

GetNetworkListImpl consumes adapter metadata and unicast addresses only.
Do not collect anycast, multicast, DNS server or DNS suffix information.
This avoids DNS-service RPCs and can keep the response in the initial buffer.
Connection-type initialization remains synchronous and retains its semantics.
diff --git a/net/base/network_interfaces_win.cc b/net/base/network_interfaces_win.cc
index d273eaaf76f75..e07bd52b3ac84 100644
--- a/net/base/network_interfaces_win.cc
+++ b/net/base/network_interfaces_win.cc
@@ -236,5 +236,9 @@ bool GetNetworkList(NetworkInterfaceList* networks, int policy) {
   ULONG len = INITIAL_BUFFER_SIZE;
-  ULONG flags = 0;
+  // GetNetworkListImpl only consumes unicast addresses and adapter metadata.
+  // Avoid collecting unused address lists and DNS configuration, which can
+  // require cross-process calls and force a second call with a larger buffer.
+  ULONG flags = GAA_FLAG_SKIP_ANYCAST | GAA_FLAG_SKIP_MULTICAST |
+                GAA_FLAG_SKIP_DNS_SERVER | GAA_FLAG_SKIP_DNS_INFO;
   // Initial buffer allocated on stack.
   char initial_buf[INITIAL_BUFFER_SIZE];
   // Dynamic buffer in case initial buffer isn't large enough.
